From 5333a63ac7fea7082b497f075747362172748e82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:34:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/adreno: add SM6225 A610 speed-bin fuse values

The A610 speed-bin table only carries the SM6115 (Bengal) fuse
encodings. The shipping SM6225 (Khaje) device tree keys its GPU
power levels by the same gpu_speed_bin fuse, with the bins in
descending performance order: 0 (up to 1260 MHz), 235
(1114.8 MHz), 216 (1025 MHz), 157 (745 MHz) and 127 (600 MHz).
157 and 127 already exist in the Bengal table in the same slots
(3 and 4); add 235 and 216 as speedbins 1 and 2 so Khaje OPP
tables can use the same opp-supported-hw indices.

Without this, fuse_to_supp_hw() finds no match on Khaje units
fused 235/216 and falls back to BIT(0), exposing the fastest
bin's OPPs to slower parts. The frequency limits themselves
live in the DT OPP table; this only teaches the fuse decoder.

Identification is unchanged: the driver derives the chip-id
from the qcom,adreno-610.0 compatible, so the 0x06010001
revision reported by the vendor tree ("Adreno610v2") still
selects this A610 entry. Whether that silicon needs quirks of
its own is not addressed here.

Compile-tested only; not verified on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Port <port@local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
index a763fe5d6..a7091324b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -691,14 +691,17 @@ static const struct adreno_info a6xx_gpus[] = {
 		/*
 		 * There are (at least) three SoCs implementing A610: SM6125
 		 * (trinket), SM6115 (bengal) and SM6225 (khaje). Trinket does
-		 * not have speedbinning, as only a single SKU exists and we
-		 * don't support khaje upstream yet.  Hence, this matching
-		 * table is only valid for bengal.
+		 * not have speedbinning, as only a single SKU exists. Bengal
+		 * and Khaje encode speedbins 1 and 2 differently in the fuse
+		 * (206/200 vs 235/216), so list both encodings; the remaining
+		 * values are shared.
 		 */
 		.speedbins = ADRENO_SPEEDBINS(
 			{ 0,   0 },
 			{ 206, 1 },
+			{ 235, 1 },
 			{ 200, 2 },
+			{ 216, 2 },
 			{ 157, 3 },
 			{ 127, 4 },
 		),
